WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.452 --> 00:00:03.407
- Right.

00:00:03.407 --> 00:00:07.603
(upbeat music)

00:00:07.603 --> 00:00:09.696
I have never had American-made poutine.

00:00:10.676 --> 00:00:12.227
I don't know what they think poutine is.

00:00:12.227 --> 00:00:13.913
- People call it disco fries here

00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:15.051
and that turns me off.

00:00:16.971 --> 00:00:18.283
- I remember this looking better.

00:00:18.283 --> 00:00:19.807
Smells a bit like gasoline.

00:00:19.807 --> 00:00:22.428
Is that, should I,
should I be eating this?

00:00:22.428 --> 00:00:23.972
- Very gelatinous.

00:00:23.972 --> 00:00:25.685
- OK, here we go, here we go.

00:00:27.122 --> 00:00:29.417
- The cheese curds look
like they're shredded.

00:00:29.417 --> 00:00:30.372
- It doesn't taste awful,

00:00:30.372 --> 00:00:31.977
but it's kinda got the texture of glue.

00:00:31.977 --> 00:00:33.704
- This is terrible (chuckles).

00:00:33.704 --> 00:00:35.980
- I would pay like three dollars

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:37.951
at the most for this, Canadian.

00:00:37.951 --> 00:00:39.475
- I would not pay anything for this.

00:00:39.475 --> 00:00:41.213
You would have to pay me to eat this.

00:00:41.213 --> 00:00:42.391
(cash register)

00:00:42.391 --> 00:00:45.012
- No.
(laughing)

00:00:45.012 --> 00:00:46.658
- What?

00:00:49.258 --> 00:00:50.358
- This one's got a garnish.

00:00:50.358 --> 00:00:52.593
- This one doesn't have cheese curds.

00:00:52.593 --> 00:00:54.747
- I don't think poutine
should have a garnish.

00:00:54.747 --> 00:00:56.834
- I mean, there's no discernible gravy.

00:00:56.834 --> 00:00:58.386
There's no discernible cheese curds.

00:00:58.386 --> 00:01:00.865
- This is also terrible.

00:01:00.865 --> 00:01:03.526
- The fries are well done, which I like.

00:01:03.526 --> 00:01:05.942
- I'd pay three bucks for this.

00:01:05.942 --> 00:01:06.932
(cash register)

00:01:06.932 --> 00:01:08.143
- I mean, that's ridiculous.

00:01:08.143 --> 00:01:10.303
Poutine is like a snack food.

00:01:12.329 --> 00:01:14.645
- Oo, there's chunks of meat in here.

00:01:14.645 --> 00:01:15.620
- Way too meaty.

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:16.555
- I feel like I'm gonna regret

00:01:16.555 --> 00:01:17.367
learning what this was.

00:01:17.367 --> 00:01:18.343
- The meat is great.

00:01:18.343 --> 00:01:19.724
- Fine, hard to mess up.

00:01:19.724 --> 00:01:23.584
Not my favorite, but you know, edible.

00:01:23.584 --> 00:01:25.393
- If my goal is eat poutine,

00:01:25.393 --> 00:01:26.440
this is not it.

00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:27.580
(cash register)

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:30.295
- Why is poutine so expensive here?

00:01:30.295 --> 00:01:32.956
Are they importing everything from Quebec?

00:01:32.956 --> 00:01:34.245
It doesn't taste like it.

00:01:35.211 --> 00:01:37.073
- This is not poutine.

00:01:37.073 --> 00:01:37.906
- You tried, America.

00:01:37.906 --> 00:01:39.004
I think that's the important part.

00:01:39.004 --> 00:01:42.072
- I feel bad for my American friends

00:01:42.072 --> 00:01:45.343
that have to try this and this is what

00:01:45.343 --> 00:01:46.724
they think poutine is.

00:01:46.724 --> 00:01:48.692
- This has made me a little homesick.

00:01:50.031 --> 00:01:51.104
And a little tummy sick.

00:01:51.104 --> 00:01:52.573
- That was a thing that happened.

00:01:55.229 --> 00:01:58.770
Nope. (chuckles)

